output:
The sum of the probabilities of all possible outcomes must be equal to 1.

Therefore, the probability of the spinner landing on $C$ is equal to 

\begin{align*}
1 - \text{probability of landing on } A - \text{probability of landing on } B &= 1 - \frac{1}{3} - \frac{5}{12} \\
&= 1 - \frac{4}{12} - \frac{5}{12} \\
&= 1 - \frac{9}{12} \\
&= \frac{12}{12} - \frac{9}{12} \\
&= \frac{3}{12} \\
&= \boxed{\frac{1}{4}}
\end{align*} The answer is: \frac{1}{4}

