First, let's find the value of $k(4)$:
\begin{align*}
k(4) &= 4-5 \\
&= -1
\end{align*}

Next, we can find the value of $g(k(4))$:
\begin{align*}
g(k(4)) &= 2(-1)^2 + 2(-1) -1 \\
&= 2+(-2)-1 \\
&= -1
\end{align*}

Then, we find the value of $h(g(k(4)))$:
\begin{align*}
h(g(k(4))) &= (-1) +3 \\
&= 2
\end{align*}

Now we can find the value of $f(h(g(k(4))))$:
\begin{align*}
f(h(g(k(4)))) &= (2)^2 + 1 \\
&= 4 + 1 \\
&= 5
\end{align*}

Finally, we can find the value of $q(f(h(g(k(4)))))$:
\begin{align*}
q(f(h(g(k(4))))) &= (5)^3 \\
&= 5 \cdot 5 \cdot 5 \\
&= 125
\end{align*}

Therefore, the value of $q(f(h(g(k(4)))))$ is $\boxed{125}$. The answer is: 125

