\cos x &= \sin 4 \\
&= \cos \left( \frac{\pi}{2} - 4 \right) \\
&= \cos \left( 4 - \frac{\pi}{2} \right).
\end{align*}Since $0 \le 4 - \frac{\pi}{2} \le \pi,$ $x = \boxed{4-\frac{\pi}{2}}.$ The answer is: 4-\frac{\pi}{2}

Let $y$ equal the number of hours driven at 30 mph in the morning. Then, $y$ hours were at 30 mph, and $7-y$ hours were at 18 mph. The total distance covered is 156 miles. Using $d=r\cdot t$, the equation becomes: \begin{align*}
30(y)+18(7-y)&=156\\
\Rightarrow\qquad 30y+126-18y&=156\\
\Rightarrow\qquad 12y&=30\\
\Rightarrow\qquad y&=30/12=\boxed{\frac{5}{2}}
\end{align*} The answer is: \frac{5}{2}

