A triangle with base $b$ and height $h$ has area $(1/2)bh$. If we rearrange this triangle to form a parallelogram, the base remains unchanged and the height becomes twice as tall because it will consist of two heights from the two original triangles. The area of this parallelogram is $bh$, realizing the base-height dimensions of the original triangle. Therefore, the area of the parallelogram is $7 \times (2 \times 4) = \boxed{56}$ square inches. The answer is: 56

