Expanding $(2m + 3)(4m^2 - 2m + 1)$ yields \begin{align*}
&2m(4m^2)+2m(-2m)+2m(1) +3(4m^2)+3(-2m)+3(1) \\
&\qquad = Im^3 + Jm^2 + Km + L .\end{align*}Computing the products on the left side we get \[8m^3-4m^2+2m+12m^2-6m+3 = Im^3 + Jm^2 + Km + L .\]Simplifying the left side results in \[8m^3+8m^2-4m+3 = Im^3 + Jm^2 + Km + L,\]hence $I=8$, $J=8$, $K=-4$, and $L=3$ and therefore $$I+J+K+L=8+8-4+3=\boxed{15}.$$ The answer is: 15

