First of all, we know that $LW = LV + VW = 5 + VW.$ According to the Power of a Point theorem, $(LV)(LW) = (LM)^2$ gives us $5(LW) = (VW - 5)^2.$

[asy]
unitsize(2 cm);

pair V, W, Z, L, M;

M = dir(40);
L = M + dir(-30);
W = dir(200);
