Let $17b$ be the multiple we seek. Thus $$17b\equiv -3\pmod{53}.$$ Multiplying both sides of this equation by $4$, then reducing modulo $53$, gives: \begin{align*}
68b &\equiv -12 \pmod{53} \\
15b &\equiv -12 \pmod{53}
\end{align*} Multiplying both sides by $28$, then reducing again, gives: \begin{align*}
420b &\equiv -336 \pmod{53} \\
b &\equiv -336+318 = -18 \pmod{53}
\end{align*} Adding $53$ to $-18$ to get a positive remainder, we have $b \equiv 35 \pmod{53}$. The smallest positive solution is $b=35$, giving $17b=\boxed{595}$. (Indeed, we can check that $595 = 11\cdot 53 - 3$.) The answer is: 595

