First, we calculate $(7.8)^2$:
\begin{align*}
(7.8)^2 &= 60.84
\end{align*}

Next, we find $\lfloor 7.8 \rfloor$:
\begin{align*}
\lfloor 7.8 \rfloor &= 7
\end{align*}

Now, we substitute the values into the given expression:
\begin{align*}
\lfloor (7.8)^2 \rfloor - \lfloor 7.8 \rfloor \cdot \lfloor 7.8 \rfloor &= \lfloor 60.84 \rfloor - 7 \cdot 7 \\
&= 60 - 49 \\
&= 11
\end{align*}

Therefore, the final answer is $\boxed{11}$. The answer is: 11

