\begin{align*} 1 \qquad \frac 14 \qquad \frac 1{16} \qquad \frac 1{64} \qquad &\cdots\\ \frac 18 \qquad \frac 1{32} \qquad \frac 1{128} \qquad &\cdots\\ \frac 1{64} \qquad \frac 1{256} \qquad &\cdots\\ \frac 1{512} \qquad &\cdots\\ &\ddots \end{align*}
As a rule, the leading number of a row is $\frac{1}{2t}$ of the first number of the row above it, and every consecutive element within a row is $\frac 1t$ of its immediate predecessor. Identify the remainder of the sum of the numerator and denominator of the simplified sum of all elements within a $\frac{1}{2008}$-matrix upon division by $2008$.

