instruction:
Please solve the following problem and put your answer at the end with "The answer is: ".

In triangle $ABC$, angle $ACB$ is 50 degrees, and angle $CBA$ is 70 degrees.  Let $D$ be the foot of the perpendicular from $A$ to $BC$, $O$ the center of the circle circumscribed about triangle $ABC$, and $E$ the other end of the diameter which goes through $A$.  Find the angle $DAE$, in degrees.

[asy]

unitsize(1.5 cm);

pair A, B, C, D, E, O;

A = dir(90);

B = dir(90 + 100);

C = dir(90 - 140);

D = (A + reflect(B,C)*(A))/2;

E = -A;

O = (0,0);

draw(Circle(O,1));

draw(A--B--C--cycle);

draw(A--D);

draw(A--E,dashed);

label("$A$", A, N);

label("$B$", B, W);

label("$C$", C, SE);

label("$D$", D, SW);

label("$E$", E, S);

dot("$O$", O, dir(0));

[/asy]

