We know from the previous problem that
\begin{align*}
\sum_{k = 1}^n \frac{2a_k - 1}{a_k^2 - a_k + 1} &= 6.\\
\end{align*}
So, we can express the given sum as
\begin{align*}
2\sum_{k = 1}^n \frac{a_k}{a_k^2 - a_k + 1} - n &= 2\sum_{k = 1}^n \left(\frac{a_k}{a_k^2 - a_k + 1} - \frac{1}{2}\right) \\
&= 2\sum_{k = 1}^n \frac{2a_k - 1}{a_k^2 - a_k + 1} - n \\
&= 2 \cdot 6 - n \\
&= 12 - n.\\
\end{align*}
Hence, the answer is $\boxed{12 - n}$. The answer is: 12 - n

